'''Nova Esports''' is a [[:Category:Hong Kong|Hong Kongese]] esports organization. They have ''Arena of Valor'' and ''Honor of Kings'' division. Nova ''Honor of Kings'' team joins Honor of Kings franchise league, [[Korea King Pro League/2019/Spring|KRKPL]] in 2019 and [[King Pro League Global Tour/2020/Spring/Upper Division|KPLGT]] in 2020 with professional Honor of Kings rosters.

In 2019, [[Korea King Pro League/2019/Spring|KRKPL]] has announced the arrival of non-Korean organizations participating in KRKPL Spring 2019, including '''Nova Esports''' as an European representative. As the initial announcement, they included two European players, [[iFlekzz]] and [[Poseidon]], who have been participating in Arena of Valor tournament with [[Nova Esports EU]] before. However, due to an unforeseen circumstance, the players couldn't participate and were replaced later on.

On February 21, 2026, '''Nova Esports''' announced they entered into a partnership with ''ROC Esports''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/DVBHuAjj2p4/|title=NOVA By ROC Esports hadir dengan nama baru namun masih mengekalkan roster juara KIS4!|trans_title=NOVA by ROC Esports comes with a new name but still retains the champion KIS4 roster!|author=[[Nova Esports]]|language={{flag|my}} Bahasa Malaysia|date=2026-02-21}}</ref> On March 10, it was announced that the roster has officially been acquired by ''ROC Esports''. They will keep the name till the end of the split.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/DVBHuAjj2p4/|title=We would like to officially announce that the Nova Esports Honor of Kings International roster has been acquired and integrated into ROC Esports.|author=[[Nova Esports]]|date=2026-03-10}}</ref>

